meta {
  name: Sessions - Send Message (Stream)
  type: http
  seq: 14
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v1/workspaces/:workspace/agents/:agent/sessions/:session/messages/stream
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

params:path {
  workspace: {{workspaceId}}
  agent: {{agentId}}
  session: {{agentSessionId}}
}

headers {
  Accept: text/event-stream
}

body:json {
  {
    "message": "A customer says their invoice is wrong. What should I do?"
  }
}

docs {
  The same turn `Sessions - Send Message` runs, delivered as server-sent
  events token by token instead of one reply at the end. Requires the
  `agent.chat` permission.

  Event names on the wire:

  - `delta` — a chunk of assistant text; concatenate in the order received.
  - `tool-call` — the agent decided to call a tool (`id`, `name`,
    `arguments`).
  - `tool-result` — that tool returned (`id`, `name`).
  - `complete` — the turn finished; carries `run_id`, `status`,
    `message_id` and `text` so a client can reconcile against the REST
    transcript.
  - `error` — the turn failed. The run is marked failed before this is
    sent, so no client cleanup is needed.
  - `done` — always last, whether the turn succeeded or failed.

  The transcript is persisted by the runner whether or not anyone is
  listening, so a dropped connection loses the live view, never the
  conversation.

  Bruno renders the stream as the raw event text rather than a JSON body —
  this response is not wrapped in the usual envelope.
}
